type: software
title: "大模型的小练习（四）：朗顿蚂蚁的倒放门槛"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
authors:
  - name: "yutitan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yutitan/langton-reverse-thresholds"
url: "https://github.com/yutitan/langton-reverse-thresholds"
abstract: >-
  Reverse-play thresholds for Langton's ant: how many initial black cells are
  needed so that the ant walks, contiguously, a reversed copy of the standard
  104-step highway turn word. We record the exact ladder L_0=32, L_1=58,
  L_2=87, L_3>=88 (the single-cell value is a full-plane Lean theorem; the
  two-cell upper bound uses an external enumeration over the upstream
  two-black-cell reduction), the exact depth-distinguishability thresholds
  A_j + 104k + 1 on the 22 single-cell rays (A_j between 4,978 and 5,082;
  the final composition induction is proved in Lean), a 14-cell witness that
  walks 2,453 standard forward turns and then 119 reverse turns, the family
  12K+2 initial cells reversing K periods for every K>=1, two necessary
  conditions for a three-cell complete period, the bounded-preamble values
  12K+6 and 13, and the supply inequalities 6K <= m+u+9n+15h+12 and
  9K <= m+u+7n+14h+15. Whether three cells can reverse one complete period
  remains open; M_104 is in [3,12], M_208 is in [3,20], and D(3)>=285,176
  with finiteness open. The repository contains the Lean 4.30 formalization,
  C++/Python checkers, data tables and an independent verification report.
keywords:
  - Langton's ant
  - cellular automata
  - reverse play
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Lean 4
  - AI-assisted exploration
license: MIT
notes: >-
  Series: 大模型的小练习（四） (LLM Exercises IV); previous entries are
  https://github.com/yutitan/wowii-conjecture-138 (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24540807),
  https://github.com/yutitan/langton-ant-three-rows (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24540968)
  and https://github.com/yutitan/langton-ant-square-bound (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24541703).
  Derived with GPT 6.2 Astra (OpenAI Codex, model gpt-6.2-astra) on 2026-11-27 and
  independently verified with DeepSeek Harness; see PROVENANCE.md. This is a
  public record of a personal AI-assisted exploration and makes no priority
  claim. Depends on the fixed upstream project
  https://github.com/imfinn/langton-two-black at commit
  95e896e3035e992e48ce9d28a5ded8568c86e835 and on H. Ke's one-black-cell
   theorem (https://www.kehao.me/papers/langtons-ant-one-black/).
